<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$75 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$75 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian commercial paper market saw three promissory note tenders totalling A$75.0 million on Thursday.</p>
<p>Lend Lease Corp made the largest issue on the day, selling A$40 million of its notes maturing December 10 at two basis points over the mid-rate for corresponding bank bills.</p>
<p>Bank bill swap reference rates have continued to fall after Wednesday's widely expected 50 basis point cut in official interest rates to 6.5 percent by the Reserve Bank.</p>
<p>The bill curve remains inverted, reflecting market hopes of a further cut in official rates.</p>
